            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/logger.cpp",
                    "line": 265,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Curious, why an interface should take care of rotation while construction.\nRespective class is anyways taking care of it while logging a message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/logger.cpp",
                    "line": 265,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Suppose a log file already exists and BMC is rebooted or `vpd-manager` restarts: This code block checks for existing log file and rotates it if required. \n\n>Respective class is anyways taking care of it while logging a message\n\nYes, that is handled inside `logMessage()` API, but suppose for some reason BMC dump is generated before `logMessage()` is called, file will not be rotated and dump may have a big log file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/logger.cpp",
                    "line": 265,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "As discussed, we only need the code till where we update \"m_currentNumEntries\". Rotation can be taken care by respective class."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/logger.cpp",
                    "line": 265,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
